#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:30
msgid "Assembly and operation"
msgstr "Assembly and operation"

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:32
msgid ""
"The existing component graph exposes an optional static library. External CPU"
" Runtime consumers select the component explicitly; the Runtime does not "
"generate a SoC, Board, physical instance or factory. A future physical typed "
"factory may return an existing controller object; it must not discover a "
"target or substitute an endpoint for a controller. Caller-authored 48-bit "
"PIDs and conservative dynamic addresses are policy, not runtime names or "
"factory IDs."
msgstr ""
"The existing component graph exposes an optional static library. External CPU"
" Runtime consumers select the component explicitly; the Runtime does not "
"generate a SoC, Board, physical instance or factory. A future physical typed "
"factory may return an existing controller object; it must not discover a "
"target or substitute an endpoint for a controller. Caller-authored 48-bit "
"PIDs and conservative dynamic addresses are policy, not runtime names or "
"factory IDs."

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:39
msgid ""
"Construction validates representable, aligned and separate controller, "
"target, event and policy storage, duplicate PIDs/addresses, every required "
"port leaf and a service batch of 1..8 B before claiming hardware. Rejection "
"retains no storage or hardware ownership. The port must uniquely claim the "
"controller, IRQs, clock and pins. Successful claim also asserts an "
"independently established baseline proof that every target dynamic address is"
" invalidated, including targets that stayed powered across MCU reset. The "
"caller establishes that proof before construction; a missing proof rejects "
"without attempting reset or retaining ownership. Its context and supplied "
"storage must outlive every observer. The caller must keep complete port/clock"
" context spans separate from all request, payload and output storage; the "
"core has no declared context extents with which to prove those aliases."
msgstr ""
"Construction validates representable, aligned and separate controller, "
"target, event and policy storage, duplicate PIDs/addresses, every required "
"port leaf and a service batch of 1..8 B before claiming hardware. Rejection "
"retains no storage or hardware ownership. The port must uniquely claim the "
"controller, IRQs, clock and pins. Successful claim also asserts an "
"independently established baseline proof that every target dynamic address is"
" invalidated, including targets that stayed powered across MCU reset. The "
"caller establishes that proof before construction; a missing proof rejects "
"without attempting reset or retaining ownership. Its context and supplied "
"storage must outlive every observer. The caller must keep complete port/clock"
" context spans separate from all request, payload and output storage; the "
"core has no declared context extents with which to prove those aliases."

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:52
msgid ""
"Initialize unused request metadata with `nx_request_initialize`, then prepare"
" an explicit DISCOVER, PRIVATE or supported CCC request. Use an absolute "
"deadline in the injected clock domain; `NX_DEADLINE_NEVER` is explicit."
msgstr ""
"Initialize unused request metadata with `nx_request_initialize`, then prepare"
" an explicit DISCOVER, PRIVATE or supported CCC request. Use an absolute "
"deadline in the injected clock domain; `NX_DEADLINE_NEVER` is explicit."

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:55
msgid ""
"Submit the request. A rejection leaves the caller's request and output ticket"
" unborrowed and unchanged by admission. Successful admission borrows request "
"metadata and payload; TX data remain immutable."
msgstr ""
"Submit the request. A rejection leaves the caller's request and output ticket"
" unborrowed and unchanged by admission. Successful admission borrows request "
"metadata and payload; TX data remain immutable."

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:58
msgid ""
"Call `nx_i3c_service` from the same executor. One call performs one aggregate"
" FIFO/event observation with at most the selected payload batch capacity, or "
"one quiescence proof. Protocol identity and copied-event metadata have their "
"own fixed port bounds. The port cannot retain command/span pointers or call "
"the application. `transferred` counts bytes handed to/from the FIFO, not "
"proven target side effects; errors never trigger replay."
msgstr ""
"Call `nx_i3c_service` from the same executor. One call performs one aggregate"
" FIFO/event observation with at most the selected payload batch capacity, or "
"one quiescence proof. Protocol identity and copied-event metadata have their "
"own fixed port bounds. The port cannot retain command/span pointers or call "
"the application. `transferred` counts bytes handed to/from the FIFO, not "
"proven target side effects; errors never trigger replay."

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:64
msgid ""
"Read results only after acquire-observing SETTLED. Cancellation and timeout "
"request withdrawal and preserve the borrow. Frame completion first enters "
"DRAINING. Only actual wire, FIFO, IRQ and port-observer quiescence permits "
"the core to detach all references and release-publish SETTLED as its final "
"request access. Failed proof enters QUARANTINED; keep request and payload "
"alive and continue explicit recovery/service."
msgstr ""
"Read results only after acquire-observing SETTLED. Cancellation and timeout "
"request withdrawal and preserve the borrow. Frame completion first enters "
"DRAINING. Only actual wire, FIFO, IRQ and port-observer quiescence permits "
"the core to detach all references and release-publish SETTLED as its final "
"request access. Failed proof enters QUARANTINED; keep request and payload "
"alive and continue explicit recovery/service."

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:71
msgid ""
"PRIVATE transfers contain 1..65535 B. The CCC whitelist permits ENEC/DISEC "
"writes and direct GETMWL/GETMRL/GETPID/GETBCR/GETDCR/GETSTATUS reads with "
"their defined lengths. Address mutation, HDR, controller handoff and legacy "
"I2C are excluded. The core does not interpret product registers or own "
"external recovery policy."
msgstr ""
"PRIVATE transfers contain 1..65535 B. The CCC whitelist permits ENEC/DISEC "
"writes and direct GETMWL/GETMRL/GETPID/GETBCR/GETDCR/GETSTATUS reads with "
"their defined lengths. Address mutation, HDR, controller handoff and legacy "
"I2C are excluded. The core does not interpret product registers or own "
"external recovery policy."

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:76
msgid "Discovery identities and reset"
msgstr "Discovery identities and reset"

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:78
msgid ""
"DISCOVER is finite and explicit. Each observed PID must match the authored "
"table. Before requesting an assignment, the core increments that target's "
"nonwrapping epoch and records its address as tentative. Only the subsequent "
"hardware assignment acknowledgement confirms the endpoint. An observation can"
" acknowledge the preceding target and announce the next identity; the core "
"confirms first. Unknown, duplicate or malformed identities and incomplete "
"assignments fault admission. Epoch exhaustion rejects a new incarnation "
"rather than wrapping."
msgstr ""
"DISCOVER is finite and explicit. Each observed PID must match the authored "
"table. Before requesting an assignment, the core increments that target's "
"nonwrapping epoch and records its address as tentative. Only the subsequent "
"hardware assignment acknowledgement confirms the endpoint. An observation can"
" acknowledge the preceding target and announce the next identity; the core "
"confirms first. Unknown, duplicate or malformed identities and incomplete "
"assignments fault admission. Epoch exhaustion rejects a new incarnation "
"rather than wrapping."

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:86
msgid ""
"A partial DAA failure, cancellation, deadline, controller reset or failed "
"drain must retain every confirmed and tentative dynamic address. It must not "
"clear the table or reuse an address that may still be held by a target. "
"Closed admission is required for `nx_i3c_reset`. Its external port proof must"
" establish both wire/ FIFO/IRQ/observer quiescence and invalidation of "
"**every target's dynamic address**. A peripheral reset or FIFO flush alone "
"cannot return SUCCESS. A failed proof retains all requests and records. "
"Successful proof invalidates endpoint records while preserving their epoch "
"counters; old endpoint and cancellation identities cannot address a later "
"incarnation. Reopen requires an idle, unfaulted controller."
msgstr ""
"A partial DAA failure, cancellation, deadline, controller reset or failed "
"drain must retain every confirmed and tentative dynamic address. It must not "
"clear the table or reuse an address that may still be held by a target. "
"Closed admission is required for `nx_i3c_reset`. Its external port proof must"
" establish both wire/ FIFO/IRQ/observer quiescence and invalidation of "
"**every target's dynamic address**. A peripheral reset or FIFO flush alone "
"cannot return SUCCESS. A failed proof retains all requests and records. "
"Successful proof invalidates endpoint records while preserving their epoch "
"counters; old endpoint and cancellation identities cannot address a later "
"incarnation. Reopen requires an idle, unfaulted controller."

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:97
msgid "Copied events and shutdown"
msgstr "Copied events and shutdown"

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:99
msgid ""
"IBI data contain at most four copied bytes. The confirmed BCR must advertise "
"IBI capability in bit1; bit2 requires 1..4 B including the mandatory data "
"byte (MDB), otherwise the event contains zero data bytes. Accepted IBI events"
" carry the exact confirmed endpoint epoch. Unknown-address, tentative, "
"unadvertised, malformed or oversized IBI observations increase a saturating "
"rejection counter. A hot-join event has no endpoint and requests caller-"
"controlled discovery; it never creates an object or starts work. The caller "
"chooses the positive ring capacity and consumes events explicitly. Overflow "
"drops only the new event, preserves queued events and increments a saturating"
" overflow counter. There is no timestamp or loss-free delivery claim."
msgstr ""
"IBI data contain at most four copied bytes. The confirmed BCR must advertise "
"IBI capability in bit1; bit2 requires 1..4 B including the mandatory data "
"byte (MDB), otherwise the event contains zero data bytes. Accepted IBI events"
" carry the exact confirmed endpoint epoch. Unknown-address, tentative, "
"unadvertised, malformed or oversized IBI observations increase a saturating "
"rejection counter. A hot-join event has no endpoint and requests caller-"
"controlled discovery; it never creates an object or starts work. The caller "
"chooses the positive ring capacity and consumes events explicitly. Overflow "
"drops only the new event, preserves queued events and increments a saturating"
" overflow counter. There is no timestamp or loss-free delivery claim."

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:109
msgid ""
"Close prevents admission while keeping active loans, address records and "
"events. Stop closes and withdraws active work, returns BUSY while requests or"
" events remain, and returns STATE while faulted or assigned/tentative "
"addresses remain. In that state, the caller must explicitly obtain the whole-"
"bus reset proof before final stop; final proven quiescence then permits "
"release of the physical claim. The controller storage is a permanent "
"identity/tombstone after stop and cannot be reconstructed; it and copied "
"ticket/endpoint storage must remain valid until external controls have "
"joined. Product code owns scheduling, service frequency, recovery decisions "
"and the final shutdown sequence."
msgstr ""
"Close prevents admission while keeping active loans, address records and "
"events. Stop closes and withdraws active work, returns BUSY while requests or"
" events remain, and returns STATE while faulted or assigned/tentative "
"addresses remain. In that state, the caller must explicitly obtain the whole-"
"bus reset proof before final stop; final proven quiescence then permits "
"release of the physical claim. The controller storage is a permanent "
"identity/tombstone after stop and cannot be reconstructed; it and copied "
"ticket/endpoint storage must remain valid until external controls have "
"joined. Product code owns scheduling, service frequency, recovery decisions "
"and the final shutdown sequence."

#: docs/design/i3c-controller.md:119
msgid ""
"Construction checks duplicate identities/addresses in O(target_count²). DAA "
"and IBI lookups scan the explicit target count; ring operations are O(1). "
"Each service pump handles at most the selected 1..8 B batch, one IBI and one "
"hot-join observation. Caller storage grows with target count, event capacity "
"and exact request/payload sizes. These are software bounds, not measured wire"
" latency."
msgstr ""
"Construction checks duplicate identities/addresses in O(target_count²). DAA "
"and IBI lookups scan the explicit target count; ring operations are O(1). "
"Each service pump handles at most the selected 1..8 B batch, one IBI and one "
"hot-join observation. Caller storage grows with target count, event capacity "
"and exact request/payload sizes. These are software bounds, not measured wire"
" latency."

